RBAC-3 'cannot start' evidence — scripts/rbac_verify.py against production
base-url: https://api.tracelab.aquex.ai    date: 2026-09-16
Each case below MUST exit non-zero with a named, actionable reason. A run that
cannot start reporting nothing is the exact silence that cost five sprints.

### Case 1: no credentials configured (scheduled run with missing secrets)
CANNOT START: no verification credentials. Set RBAC_VERIFY_USERNAME and RBAC_VERIFY_PASSWORD to a dedicated verification identity (preferred), or AUTH_USERNAME and AUTH_PASSWORD. Both the username and the password must be set; AUTH_USERNAME was empty and its password was empty.
exit=2

### Case 2: the stale bare username from the repo's local .env (the Sprint 49-54 silent case)
CANNOT START: AUTH_USERNAME='kneelinghorse' is a bare username, not an email address. This harness no longer derives kneelinghorse@tracelab.local — that derivation is why every run since Sprint 49 authenticated as the fabricated bootstrap account instead of a real one. Set AUTH_USERNAME to the full email address of the verification identity.
exit=2

### Case 3: the retired bootstrap identity spelled out in full
CANNOT START: AUTH_USERNAME='kneelinghorse@tracelab.local' is the retired bootstrap identity at the non-routable domain @tracelab.local. Sprint 55 RBAC-1 demoted that account precisely so verification would stop depending on it. Set RBAC_VERIFY_USERNAME and RBAC_VERIFY_PASSWORD to a dedicated verification identity with a real, routable address.
exit=2
